# Gran Pulse Ochu ({G}, 1/1 deathtouch): "{8}: Until end of turn, this creature gets +1/+1 for each permanent card in your graveyard."
# On turn 3 two Black Lotuses are sacrificed for the {8} (with Mox Jet and Mox Ruby), and the graveyard also holds an instant
# card, Lightning Bolt, which is not a permanent card (CR 110.4a), while Bot2's graveyard holds Bot2's own Black Lotus, which is
# not in "your graveyard": the count is two, so Gran Pulse Ochu is a 3/3 (CR 608.2h). The {8} is paid exactly: six from the
# Lotuses, one each from Mox Jet and Mox Ruby, the pool empty and Mox Emerald left untapped. The Wall of
# Bot2, 0/4, blocks it and takes three damage, not enough to destroy it: deathtouch does (CR 702.2b). On turn 4 it is a 1/1 again.

